From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olexandr Tyshchenko <o.tyshchenko@eslua.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mali valhall: list_count_nodes() is in 6.1.191 and later

Linux 6.1.191 backported list_count_nodes() to include/linux/list.h.
The Mali Valhall compatibility header defined its own copy for every
kernel before 6.3, which no longer builds.
---
diff --git a/include/linux/version_compat_defs_for_valhall.h b/include/linux/version_compat_defs_for_valhall.h
index 685067ae8..51ade45c3 100644
--- a/include/linux/version_compat_defs_for_valhall.h
+++ b/include/linux/version_compat_defs_for_valhall.h
@@ -619,7 +619,8 @@ static inline void kbase_lockdep_assert_not_held(struct mutex *lock)
 #endif
 }
 
-#if KERNEL_VERSION(6, 3, 0) > LINUX_VERSION_CODE
+#if KERNEL_VERSION(6, 1, 191) > LINUX_VERSION_CODE || \
+	(KERNEL_VERSION(6, 2, 0) <= LINUX_VERSION_CODE && KERNEL_VERSION(6, 3, 0) > LINUX_VERSION_CODE)
 static inline size_t list_count_nodes(struct list_head *head)
 {
 	struct list_head *pos;
-- 
2.47.3
